[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged every report about wrong dates into one ticket, because
[decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line alone. The reports
describe two problems with two different fixes, so each one now has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
The fix queued for #4471 fixes the parser. It does not touch the booking-v3 form hint,
so those reports keep coming after it ships.
</Callout>

## The split

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} issues={{ parser: 'https://github.com/poponuts/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1', hint: 'https://github.com/poponuts/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2', shift: 'https://github.com/poponuts/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/3' }} />

## How to tell them apart

- **parser**: a day-first tenant, and the day and month in the report swap (7 April became 4 July).
  The report came by app, by email, or through a booking-v2 form.
- **hint**: the same swap, but through the booking form of a booking-v3 tenant. That form prints
  `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, so people type the month first, and the form reads the tenant's
  way. Fixing the parser does not fix this one; the form hint has to change.
- **shift**: a few reports describe a one-day move, not a swap ("Lisbon got Tuesday, Toronto got
  Monday"). The desk reads them as one-day moves (`desk-notes.json`) and counts them where their
  cause files them, under `parser`; their ticket is closed as a duplicate of the parser ticket.

Read the report body and the tenant, not the intake tag: intake guesses from the reporter's
browser, and its tag disagrees with the cause on dozens of these reports.

